    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nVim 9.0 flattens blockwise registers into linear newline-delimited inserts for both methods, whereas Neovim nightly preserves blockwise selection semantics during `<C-r>0`. Is this intentional?\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. echo -n \"first\\nsecond\" | nvim\n2. `<C-v>jy`\n3. `i<C-r>0` or `i<C-r>\"`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`i_CTRL-R_0` should also insert text linearly.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1596+g28ff47b8a4\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, vim  9.0\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nubuntu 22.04\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nwindows terminal 1.25.1912\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nappimage",
